      "content": "[\n  {\n    \"title\": \"The Fable 5 Export Controls Harm US Cyber Defense\",\n    \"description\": \"Kate Moussouris confirms that the 'jailbreak' that led to Claude Fable 5 being banned under export controls was simply asking the model to 'fix this code' with known CVEs. This is absurd because coding models fixing bugs is crucial for defensive security - finding, fixing, and testing patches is exactly what defenders need AI to do. Non-technical decision-makers are ready to ban models that help secure code.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Kate Moussouris)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-16\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI security\", \"export controls\", \"jailbreaking\", \"cyberdefense\", \"Claude Fable 5\", \"Anthropic\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Cloudflare CAPTCHA optimization with Claude Code\",\n    \"description\": \"Used Claude Code to optimize Cloudflare CAPTCHA rules - now only triggers for search URLs containing at least one ampersand, allowing simple ?q=term searches to work without challenge. Also tried Cloudflare MCP with Claude Code but had to switch to Cloudflare API directly.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-16\",\n    \"topics\": [\"Claude Code\", \"Cloudflare\", \"CAPTCHA\", \"MCP\", \"optimization\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"datasette-agent 0.3a0 with user approval for write operations\",\n    \"description\": \"New execute_write_sql tool requests user approval before writing to database, taking user permissions into account. Enhanced datasette agent chat terminal mode supports approvals, with new --root, --yes, and --unsafe options. Can now use 'datasette agent chat content.db -m gpt-5.5 --unsafe' to directly modify databases through natural language prompts.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-15\",\n    \"topics\": [\"datasette\", \"AI agents\", \"user approval\", \"SQL\", \"tool use\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Personality clashes behind Anthropic's model suspension\",\n    \"description\": \"Behind-the-scenes reporting on US government export control of Mythos/Fable models. Anthropic's red team members (Logan Graham, Dave Orr, Nicholas Carlini) meeting with Commerce Department. Sources suggest the situation may come down to making everyone 'feel safe, secure and happy' rather than technical fixes.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Axios reporting)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-15\",\n    \"topics\": [\"Anthropic\", \"export controls\", \"jailbreaking\", \"policy\", \"Claude Mythos\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Why AI hasn't replaced software engineers, and won't\",\n    \"description\": \"Arvind Narayanan and Sayash Kappor analyze AI job displacement through the lens of software engineering. Data shows no AI-related mass layoffs (160 WARN Act filings, zero checked AI box). Real bottlenecks aren't typing code but: (1) deciding and specifying what to build, (2) verifying and being accountable for deliveries, (3) deep human understanding of codebase, business, and environment.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Arvind Narayanan and Sayash Kappor)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-14\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI employment\", \"software engineering\", \"job displacement\", \"AI capabilities\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Mapping SQLite result columns back to their source table.column\",\n    \"description\": \"Research project to programmatically identify which table.column each result column came from in arbitrary SQL queries. Used Claude Code (Opus 4.8) to explore multiple solutions: apsw, ctypes accessing sqlite3_column_table_name(), and clever interrogation of EXPLAIN output. Enables rendering Datasette queries with additional metadata.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-13\",\n    \"topics\": [\"SQLite\", \"Claude Code\", \"SQL\", \"Datasette\", \"Python\"],\n    \"type\": \"technical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"US government directive suspends Fable 5 and Mythos 5 access\",\n    \"description\": \"Anthropic received export control directive to suspend all access to Fable 5 and Mythos 5 by any foreign national due to alleged jailbreak. Government cited 'a method of bypassing' but Anthropic's review found it's just asking models to 'read a specific codebase and fix any software flaws' - capabilities widely available in other models like GPT-5.5. Access cut off at 6:59pm Pacific on June 12.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Anthropic statement)\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-13\",\n    \"topics\": [\"export controls\", \"Anthropic\", \"Claude Fable 5\", \"Claude Mythos 5\", \"government policy\", \"jailbreaking\"],\n    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"OpenAI WebRTC Audio Session with document context\",\n    \"description\": \"Enhanced OpenAI WebRTC audio tool to use GPT-Realtime-2 model (GPT-5-class reasoning) and support pasting document context for audio conversations. Enables conversational exploration of documents in browser with voice model.\",\n    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-06-12\",\n    \"topics\": [\"OpenAI\", \"WebRTC\", \"audio\", \"GPT-Realtime-2\", \"multi-modal\"],\